\pard\keep\keepn\sb160\sa120\sl240\slmult1\qj\f1\fs24 Purpose and Expected Standard\par

\pard\sa60\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0 This handbook provides fifty substantial projects that translate the complete Design and Analysis of Algorithms syllabus into industry-oriented C or C++ products. Every project is designed for an eight-week development period and requires students to move beyond a single algorithm: they must model a real problem, implement alternative strategies, prove or justify correctness, measure time and space behaviour, and explain which approach is practical under different operating conditions.\par
The title, ten-point explanation, and expected product for every project are self-contained. The Common Syllabus Implementation Standard below is mandatory for every student and forms part of every project briefly, even when a domain naturally emphasizes only some algorithms.\par

